  "unmapped_findings": [
    "Mechanical tests: Brinell hardness (62.5 g load, 2.5 mm ball); compression and tension at deformation rate 10^-4 s^-1; compression tested from room temperature up to 800 °C; tension tested at room temperature, 650 °C and 800 °C; elevated-temperature tests in protective argon with 30 min hold at test temperature (b0018, b0038, b0040).",
    "Fe-26Al-4Nb-1C is three-phase, containing Laves phase (Fe,Al)2Nb besides NbC carbides in the Fe3Al matrix (b0013).",
    "Tension-compression asymmetry observed in all investigated alloys at room temperature and elevated temperatures; Fe-26Al-based alloys show higher asymmetry than Fe-15Al-based alloys (b0029, b0040, b0045)."
  ]
}
